WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.382
The common table expression creates patient-level features.

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:09.662
Inside it, correlated scalar subqueries calculate each patient's admission count, abnormal-lab count,

00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:15.107
and distinct-medication count. The outer SELECT then calculates the synthetic score.

00:00:15.107 --> 00:00:19.932
When reading a long query, identify the row grain and feature columns first.

00:00:19.932 --> 00:00:23.272
Only then interpret the final derived expression.

00:00:23.272 --> 00:00:28.022
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:32.047
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:32.047 --> 00:00:33.897
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:33.897 --> 00:00:41.442
In a real setting such as a compliance workflow checking whether related evidence exists,

00:00:41.442 --> 00:00:46.322
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:46.322 --> 00:00:48.792
before discussing syntax.

00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:54.411
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
